    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0449" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/270: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Frost</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-16T19:00:00-05:00">March 16, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your telegram no. 31, March 12, 2 p.m. A study is being made of the
                    observations with respect to Article 11 and you may expect detailed comments in
                    a few days.</p>
                <p>With reference to the last paragraph of your telegram the Department, for reasons
                    of law and policy, is unable to accord favorable consideration to setting up a
                    commission “which could from time to time readjust the agreement”. In fact it
                    could not agree to the establishment of any commission the existence of which
                    might be construed as a delegation of the powers conferred on the President by
                    the Trade Agreements Act<anchor n="30" xml:id="d451-f1"/> or whose functions
                    might conflict with those of existing American Government agencies.
                    Nevertheless, in an effort to meet Chile’s views the Department would be
                    willing, if Chile so desires, to give consideration to setting up commissions,
                    similar to the recently established American Brazilian Mixed Commissions,<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d451-f2"/> the scope of which would be to observe the course
                    of trade between the two countries, to observe the operation of the agreement
                    and to report thereon to their Governments in their capacity as private bodies
                    entirely independent of their Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
